    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d773">

                <pb facs="0274" n="1324" xml:id="pg1324"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">690D.91/8–1353: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in
                        India</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d773-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-07-15T22:32:00-04:00">July 15, 1953—10:32
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>48. Embtel 79. You authorized give Nehru firmest assurances US Government made no
                    suggestions officially or unofficially encourage Kashmir government seek
                    satisfaction any given set demands. You may assure Nehru Stevenson given no
                    mission discuss Kashmir with Abdullah or anyone else.</p>
                <p>In light current misunderstandings among Indian officials public you may wish
                    instruct your staff refrain visits Kashmir for present.</p>
                <p>While making clear Nehru complete lack substance charges our interference Kashmir
                    you should remind him our real hope forthcoming negotiations will provide
                    progress Kashmir solution.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d773-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d773-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was repeated for information to Karachi and London.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
